# The formatter reads only the `.gitignore` at its working directory, never a nested one, so a
# root-run pass reaches every subject a nested file excludes. Each nested `.gitignore` entry that the
# root one does not already carry is repeated here. Anchored with `**/` rather than pinned to the one
# path that exists today, so a second package is excluded with no edit.

# Build and generated output.
**/dist/
**/src/wire/
**/.docusaurus/
**/.cache-loader/

# Test-runner output and staging.
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/.staged-extensions/

# Local environment files and debug logs.
**/.env.local
**/.env.development.local
**/.env.test.local
**/.env.production.local
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*

# Tracked, so no ignore file excludes it, and rewriting it produces a diff no one reads.
**/package-lock.json

# Derived JSON that a test writes verbatim and then compares byte-for-byte. The emitting code owns
# these bytes, so reformatting one does not produce a diff a reader acts on — it makes the comparison
# report a difference on every run, which is a permanently red gate rather than a formatting nit. A
# trailing newline added here is exactly how the wire-snapshot fixtures went red and stayed red.
**/Contracts/fixtures/*.json
**/wire/openapi.json
